REM Protects TABLE statements from being split into extra sibling statements that
REM falsely need a line break before or after them. Covers: with and without a
REM leading label, short and long unspaced data, spaced and mixed-spacing data,
REM upper/lower/mixed-case keyword, and a trailing ;rem comment.
TABLE ff00aa11
L1: TABLE ff00aa11
TABLE aabbccddeeff00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff0011
TABLE aa bb cc dd ee ff
TABLE aabb cc ddee ff
TABLE FF00AA11
table ff00aa11
TaBlE ff00aa11
TABLE ff00aa11;rem trailing comment
L2: table aa bb cc dd
